---
// Evidence rules — spec §8.5, binding. Two claims were available in the
// source material (the WordPress export at admoranmarketing_WordPress_2026-08-08.xml):
// a vague "ranks first for several keywords" line with no named queries or
// dated export, and no lead-attribution figure at all (the 70% example in
// the spec itself was illustrative, not real data pulled from this client).
// Neither clears the bar: "ranks for most keywords" is unverifiable by a
// reader, and there is no owner quote to attribute a lead percentage to.
// Per §8.5, the page ships without either claim. Vincent can add both once
// he has a dated GSC export with named queries and an actual quote from
// Godfrey — see the build report.
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import CTAButton from '../../components/CTAButton.astro';
import CTASection from '../../components/CTASection.astro';
import screenshot from '../../assets/decl-website.png';

const title = 'DECL Website — Environmental Consultancy Web Design Case Study | Admoran';
const description =
  'How I built the website for DECL, a Kenyan environmental consultancy specialising in ESIA and Environmental Audit, from zero online presence to a live, structured, search-ready site.';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'DECL Website — a case study',
  about: {
    '@type': 'Service',
    name: 'Web Design',
    url: 'https://admoran.com/web-design/',
  },
  author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Vincent Mbogo' },
  url: 'https://admoran.com/work/decl/',
};
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <!-- Header -->
  <section class="bg-paper">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-section px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
      <div class="max-w-prose">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-muted">Environmental consultancy &middot; Web design + SEO</p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 font-heading text-[clamp(2.25rem,4.5vw,3.5rem)] font-semibold leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-ink">
          DECL — a website built for a firm that had never needed one before.
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-6 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Diligent Environmental Consultancy Limited, a Kenyan firm specialising in Environmental
          and Social Impact Assessment (ESIA) and Environmental Audit (EA).
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://decl.co.ke/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="mt-3 inline-block font-semibold text-ink underline decoration-accent/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-accent"
        >
          decl.co.ke &rarr;
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="mx-auto mt-10 max-w-3xl">
        <Image src={screenshot} alt="The DECL website, shown on desktop and mobile" width={1000} height={650} class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-line" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The situation -->
  <section class="border-t border-line bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-section px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
      <div class="max-w-prose">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-[2rem] font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">
          The situation.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          DECL's founder, Godfrey Njugi, had built a real consultancy practice with no online
          presence and no organic lead channel — new work came entirely through referral and
          direct relationships. ESIA and EA are high-consideration, search-led purchases: a
          procurement officer, a developer, or an NGO looking for a licensed environmental
          consultant is exactly the kind of buyer who searches for one and converts from what they
          find. Without a site, that entire channel was closed off.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What I did -->
  <section class="border-t border-line bg-paper">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-section px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
      <div class="max-w-prose">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-[2rem] font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">
          What I did.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          I designed and built the site from a blank slate: a structure organised around what DECL
          actually does — ESIA, Environmental Audit, and the specific regulatory work under each —
          rather than a generic "services" page that tries to cover everything in one paragraph.
          Each service area got its own page, targeted at the specific terms a buyer searching for
          a licensed environmental consultant in Kenya would actually use.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          On the technical side: clean URL structure from launch, schema markup identifying DECL as
          a professional service provider, a responsive build that works on the mobile connections
          most Kenyan searches happen on, and Google Analytics and Search Console configured before
          launch — not bolted on once someone asked whether it was working.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What happened -->
  <section class="border-t border-line bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-section px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
      <div class="max-w-prose">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-[2rem] font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">
          What happened.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          The site has been live and indexed since 2023, giving DECL a findable presence for its
          specific service area that didn't exist before. What I don't have yet is a dated ranking
          export with named queries, or a sourced figure for how much of DECL's enquiry volume now
          comes through the site — so I'm not printing either here. A vague "ranks for most
          keywords" is a claim, not a result, and this is the page on the whole site that most
          needs to be trusted. When Godfrey and I pull a current Search Console export, the
          specific queries and positions will replace this paragraph.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What I'd do differently -->
  <section class="border-t border-line bg-paper">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-section px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
      <div class="max-w-prose">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-[2rem] font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">
          What I'd do differently.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          I'd have set up a lightweight way to track enquiry source from day one — even a simple
          "how did you hear about us" field — instead of relying on Godfrey's recollection months
          later. It's a small thing that would have made this exact case study easier to write
          honestly, sooner.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <CTASection class="border-t border-line bg-paper">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-section px-6 py-16 text-center md:py-24">
      <p class="text-[1.0625rem] text-muted">
        Want a site built the same way?
        <a href="/web-design/" class="font-semibold text-ink underline decoration-accent/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-accent">
          See web design services &rarr;
        </a>
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8">
        <CTAButton size="lg" message="Hi Vincent, I found the DECL case study on admoran.com and I'd like to talk about a website build.">
          Talk on WhatsApp
        </CTAButton>
      </div>
    </div>
  </CTASection>
</Layout>
